  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Horti and Agrofood Pavilion Lagos</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Agrofood Nigeria fair is a strategic stepping stone for the newly approved combi-track &quot;Horti&quot; in Nigeria. It allows the Netherlands to showcase itself through its private sector and ODA-paid programmes and projects. At the same time, the Dutch government can use the gathering of these actors to make concrete steps in the further development of their implementation strategy by organizing roundtables and brainstorming sessions.This project&apos;s overarching goal is to develop and improve the (increasing) existing economic ties between the Netherlands and Nigeria, particularly in the agricultural sector.The purpose of this event is to highlight Dutch knowledge and expertise in medium- to high-level horticultural production systems for urban and city farming and to develop a food roadmap for Southwest Nigeria, for further implementation under the combi-track &quot;Horti&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
